  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Life-saving assistance through the provision of emergency SNFI and WASH supplies to conflict-affected households in Western Equatoria.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The confluence of factors continues to drive humanitarian needs in South Sudan.  Conflicts, disease outbreaks and climate-induced shocks - especially floods and drought-like conditions - have widely affected South Sudan and generated humanitarian needs over the years. Acute needs are at elevated levels, and life-saving humanitarian interventions are critical. Recent armed clashes and insecurity have triggered large-scale displacement across Western Equatoria State, with more than 220,000 people estimated to have been uprooted from their homes as violence spread across multiple counties, significantly worsening the humanitarian situation and leaving internally displaced persons (IDPs) in urgent need of emergency assistance. This project seeks to mitigate a worsening humanitarian crisis through delivery of integrated, life-saving assistance. This strategic intervention focuses on essential health and nutrition services, emergency shelter and non-food items, protection support, and safe access to water and sanitation, ensuring a coordinated response that mitigates the impact of worsening conditions and restores the dignity of displaced populations.</narrative>
  </description>
